**Profile:** 
 You have at least 4 \- 6 years’ experience in financial industry, you worked with legal/corporate department of a fiduciary or have worked in a law firm or MNC. You are willing and looking to consolidate and grow your skills and talents in the long term with a company that works in a strong team and results\-based environment. You speak English fluently.




**Responsibilities**
* Manage the legal and corporate requirements for your real estate portfolios
* Ensure thorough absorption of new deals post\-closing and subsequently the management of the entities during their legal and corporate life cycle until the disposal process;
* Liaise with the cross\-London and internal management as well as service providers and advisors for the efficient running of all deals and entities’ corporate governance;
* Draft, review and ensure the accuracy of legal documents in relation to corporate law (implementation of template clauses, legislation, signature, date, corporate details etc.);
* Liaise with the Revantage finance, tax, acquisition and sales teams for transparency of information, organisation and incorporation of advice in the legal documentation;
* Organise regular board meetings, board minutes, Statutory filings, written resolutions ;
* Oversee restructuring and financing steps along with other internal and external teams and advisors;
* Help to maintain the company database and assist in the virtual archiving process ;
* Monitor the accuracy and accessibility of legal and corporate documents ;
* Ensure organized, clear and consistent saving, filing and scanning of all documents.


